    "## Ensemble mean and variance of interior solutions\n",
    "\n",
    "We now have a method for drawing boundary function samples (based on both observations and the potential, and of the field), and a method for generating the interior solution given a boundary. Putting these together, we have an ensemble of solutions, the variance of which is what we would like to study.\n",
    "\n",
    "Our interior solution is generated from Fourier coeffients, so the take an individual boundary function sample and solve it, we need to decompose the function with an FFT and serve the resulting coefficients. The `decompose` method does this, and then the sample potentials, fields, and their means and variance are computed."
   ]
